    </row>
    <row>
      <id><![CDATA[247]]></id>
      <qid><![CDATA[51]]></qid>
      <question><![CDATA[<div style="margin-bottom: 15px; padding: 10px 14px; background: #f7f9fa; border-left: 3px solid #3498db; font-size: 0.92em;"><p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>Barrier definitions:</strong></p><p style="margin: 6px 0;"><strong>Long charging time:</strong> <span style="color: #555;">Slow charging reduces vehicle availability and disrupt delivery schedules, with congestion at peak hours further delaying operations, especially for heavy-duty trucks.</span></p><p style="margin: 6px 0;"><strong>Scheduling/synchronization complexity:</strong> <span style="color: #555;">Rigid delivery schedules conflict with cost-efficient off-peak charging. Solving joint routing–charging problems is computationally complex, and autonomous systems add further coordination challenges, especially for platoon synchronization.</span></p><p style="margin: 6px 0;"><strong>Traffic and weather uncertainty:</strong> <span style="color: #555;">ADS struggle in complex traffic and adverse weather, undermining reliability and trust, while low temperatures reduce EV range and unpredictable congestion disrupts scheduling.</span></p><p style="margin: 6px 0;"><strong>Service reliability challenges:</strong> <span style="color: #555;">Unproven reliability of electric and autonomous systems threatens service levels required in freight, which operates within rigid time-windows and narrow margins.</span></p></div><p>Which is the <strong>Most challenging</strong> barrier among <em>Operational Barriers</em>?</p>]]></question>
      <help><![CDATA[]]></help>
      <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
      <script><![CDATA[]]></script>
