    <row>
      <id><![CDATA[298]]></id>
      <qid><![CDATA[61]]></qid>
      <question><![CDATA[<div style="margin-bottom: 15px; padding: 10px 14px; background: #f7f9fa; border-left: 3px solid #3498db; font-size: 0.92em;"><p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;"><strong>Barrier definitions:</strong></p><p style="margin: 6px 0;"><strong>Public acceptance concerns:</strong> <span style="color: #555;">Public skepticism stalls adoption of electrified and automated freight. This reluctance extends to key stakeholders, where misaligned priorities among OEMs, logistics operators, utilities, and governments impede coordinated investment in enabling infrastructure.</span></p><p style="margin: 6px 0;"><strong>Workforce transition challenges:</strong> <span style="color: #555;">Automation raises fears of job losses and downgraded work quality, especially for long-distance drivers, reducing acceptance. The shift toward technical roles demands new skills, but limited reskilling programs and an aging workforce intensify resistance and slow adoption.</span></p><p style="margin: 6px 0;"><strong>Safety perception concerns:</strong> <span style="color: #555;">Safety concerns for electric freight focus on battery fire and explosion risks, while autonomous systems face distrust over unexpected failures and high cybersecurity vulnerability.</span></p><p style="margin: 6px 0;"><strong>Limited public awareness:</strong> <span style="color: #555;">Insufficient understanding of automated and electric freight technologies, combined with low awareness of their benefits and resistance among drivers, constrains public acceptance and slows adoption.</span></p></div><p>Which is the <strong>Most challenging</strong> barrier among <em>Social Barriers</em>?</p>]]></question>
      <help><![CDATA[]]></help>
      <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
      <script><![CDATA[]]></script>
    </row>
    <row>
      <id><![CDATA[303]]></id>
      <qid><![CDATA[62]]></qid>
      <question><![CDATA[<p>Which is the <strong>Least challenging</strong> barrier among <em>Social Barriers</em>?</p>]]></question>
      <help><![CDATA[]]></help>
      <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
      <script><![CDATA[]]></script>
    </row>
